  "metadata": {
    "max_time_steps": 120,
    "description": "Level 3: fourteen pods, two units and a 120-step horizon - strictly more demand than the fleet can serve. Eight cheap pods cycle on an 8-step loop next door; six expensive ones sit 18 steps away behind a long aisle. Punishes both fairness and pure greed: serving the far queue at all costs strands the cheap stream, while never going costs six pods outright. Score comes from how many pods clear, weighted by decay, not from equalising lateness."
